<setup>
  <selectFromSequence name="k" from="-2" to="2" step="4"/>  
  <selectFromSequence name="a" from="-1" to="2" step="1"/>  
  <selectFromSequence name="dx" from="0.5" to="0.75" step="0.25"/> 
 
  <number name="n">4</number>
  <math name="b" simplify>$a + 4*$dx</math>

  <function name="f">3+$k*e^(-0.5*x)</function>
  <function name="F">3*x+$k*e^(-0.5*x)</function>

  <math name="L4" simplify displayDecimals="2">$dx * ($$f($a) + $$f($a+$dx) + $$f($a+2*$dx) + $$f($a+3*$dx) )</math>
  <math name="R4" simplify displayDecimals="2">$dx * ($$f($a+$dx) + $$f($a+2*$dx) + $$f($a+3*$dx) + $$f($a+4*$dx) )</math>
  <math name="M4" simplify displayDecimals="2">$dx * ($$f($a+$dx/2) + $$f($a+3*$dx/2) + $$f($a+5*$dx/2) + $$f($a+7*$dx/2))</math>
  <math name="T4" simplify>($L4 + $R4)/2</math>
  <math name="S8" simplify>(2*$M4 + $T4)/3</math>
  <math simplify name="exactInt">$$F($b) - $$F($a) </math>

</setup>
<!--
<graph xmin="-5" xmax="$m+20" ymin="-2" ymax="24">
  $c
</graph>
-->
  <p>
    Suppose we are interested in the definite integral 
    <me>
      \int_{$a}^{$b} f(x) \, dx
    </me>
    for which we know the following information:
  </p> 
  <p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          On <m>[$a,$b]</m>, <m>f</m> is either always increasing or always decreasing, and also either always concave up or always concave down.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          The left, right, and midpoint Riemann sums with <m>4</m> subintervals are <me>L_4 = $L4, \ \ R_4 = $R4, \ \ \text{and} \ \ M_4 = $M4.</me>
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>
        Determine the estimates <m>T_4</m> and <m>S_{8}</m> for the given definite integral.  
      </p>
      <p>
        <m> \int_{$a}^{$b} f(x) \, dx \approx T_4 = </m><answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.02" allowedErrorIsAbsolute> $T4</answer>
      </p>
      <p>
        <m> \int_{$a}^{$b} f(x) \, dx \approx S_8 = </m><answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.02" allowedErrorIsAbsolute> $S8</answer>
      </p>
    </li>  
    <li>
      <p>
        Is <m>f</m> increasing or decreasing on <m>[$a,$b]</m>?  concave up or concave down?  Complete the following sentence to justify your conclusions. 
      </p>
      <p>
        The function <m>f</m> is <choiceInput name="c1" inline>
          <choice>?</choice>
          <choice>always increasing</choice>
          <choice>always decreasing</choice>
        </choiceInput> because <choiceInput name="c2" inline>
          <choice>?</choice>
          <choice>the Left Riemann sum is less than the Right Riemann sum</choice>
          <choice>the Right Riemann sum is less than the Left Riemann sum</choice>
          <choice>the Trapezoid rule is less than the Midpoint rule</choice>
          <choice>the Midpoint rule is less than the Trapezoid rule</choice>
        </choiceInput>, and <m>f</m> is <choiceInput name="c3" inline>
          <choice>?</choice>
          <choice>always concave up</choice>
          <choice>always concave down</choice>
        </choiceInput> because <choiceInput name="c4" inline>
          <choice>?</choice>
          <choice>the Left Riemann sum is less than the Right Riemann sum</choice>
          <choice>the Right Riemann sum is less than the Left Riemann sum</choice>
          <choice>the Trapezoid rule is less than the Midpoint rule</choice>
          <choice>the Midpoint rule is less than the Trapezoid rule</choice>
        </choiceInput>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer><award><when>
          ($k > 0 and $c1.selectedIndices=3 and $c2.selectedIndices=3 and $c3.selectedIndices=2 and $c4.selectedIndices=5)
          or
          (0 > $k  and $c1.selectedIndices=2 and $c2.selectedIndices=2 and $c3.selectedIndices=3 and $c4.selectedIndices=4)
        </when></award></answer>
      </p>
          
          
    </li>

  </ol>  
</p>
